JavaScriptCore: cheaper value profile updates.

LLInt tier-up: while a CodeBlock's baseline plan compiled, its execution
counter stayed crossed, so every loop back edge and call took the slow path
and updated all of the CodeBlock's value profiles again. The DFG path sets a
new threshold while its plan compiles; the LLInt now does the same
(jitSoon). On a Nexus 5, YouTube's start spent 2 s in those updates.

Profile updates read each bucket three times with decodeConcurrent(), whose
sequentially consistent 64-bit load is fenced on both sides on 32-bit ARM.
Each bucket is now read once, with a relaxed atomic load; the predictions and
counts are the same. On a Nexus 5 this halved the time collections spend in
CodeBlock finalizers.

--- a/Source/JavaScriptCore/bytecode/CodeBlock.cpp
+++ b/Source/JavaScriptCore/bytecode/CodeBlock.cpp
